`verilator_config
// Waivers for the black-box substitution pass (`make lint-synth-bb`), which
// elaborates the design with syn/blackbox/*.sv in place of the behavioural
// array and the behavioural memory -- the exact source set Design Compiler
// reads.
//
// A black box is by definition a module whose ports go nowhere, so UNUSEDSIGNAL,
// UNDRIVEN and UNUSEDPARAM on those two files are not findings. They are
// waived by FILE, so the waiver cannot leak into the real design.
//
// What this pass is actually for: a stub's port list drifting from the module
// it stands in for is a PORT-NOT-FOUND error, not a warning, and no waiver
// here suppresses it. That is the failure this check exists to catch, and it is
// the one that would otherwise show up as a dc_shell error on a machine this
// repository cannot run on.

lint_off -rule UNUSEDSIGNAL -file "*syn/blackbox/*"
lint_off -rule UNDRIVEN     -file "*syn/blackbox/*"
lint_off -rule UNUSEDPARAM  -file "*syn/blackbox/*"
